{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"primitive-flowered-panther","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`rebar link <bug> <target> caused_by` refuses a target with no referencing commit through `caused_by_refusal` (`src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py:91`, called from `link_core` at line 200). A bug close with `--caused-by=<target>` writes the same `caused_by` edge through `_apply_caused_by` in `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`. That path calls `_write_link_event` directly and never consults `caused_by_refusal`. So the close accepts targets that `link` refuses, and records them with provenance `explicit`.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-03: `rebar link --dry-run frank-rocky-rat traitorous-official-sunbittern caused_by` reports \"Would reject: ... target ticket '6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa' has no commit referencing it\". frank-rocky-rat was closed with `--caused-by` aimed at that epic (a 4-hex form, see surprising-fruticose-herring), and the close wrote the edge without any such check.\n\nStory 77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed introduced the refusal and scoped it to the `link` surfaces (CLI, library, MCP, dry-run). Its plan does not mention the close path.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe escaped-defect lenses read close-written `caused_by` edges as explicit, proven attributions, but those edges skip the evidence rule that `link` enforces.\n\n## Not yet checked\n\nWhether blame-derived (`provenance: derived`) close edges should also pass `caused_by_refusal`, and how a close should behave when the check refuses (refuse the close, or close without the edge and warn).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A bug close whose explicit `--caused-by` target has no referencing commit is handled the same way `link` handles it, consistent with the policy the plan states. A unit test drives a commit-less target through `rebar.transition(..., caused_by=...)`.","id":"2651-35f7-71e2-4c8d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A bug close's --caused-by skips the no-referencing-commit refusal that rebar link enforces"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793697532110252001,"uuid":"1dac27ab-059f-4a36-bd9a-be48a9eff5d2"}